#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491191 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064341 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f270e39a-e9bc-5ad0-b8b9-34584724bc4a" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Monomial out of a Binomial Containing One Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ecfe9ff-1de0-5d94-8b8b-66524693914d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ecfe9ff-1de0-5d94-8b8b-66524693914d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490839} :answer-field/id #uuid "10e8c887-cc39-5c97-a10d-b38457e1a9d6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491009}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b304ff54-539e-5d0d-a04c-2339ab8e6486" :question/math-academy-id "q-133829" :question/problem "Expressed as a polynomial in terms of $x,$ the length of Jacob's plot of land is{{field-1}}\nmeters." :question/worked-solution "The width of the plot is $x+1$ meters, and its area is $2{x}^{2}+2x$ square meters. Since the $\\text{area}=\\text{length}\\times \\text{width},$ we factor the expression for the area to find the length.\n\nFirst, we find the $\\text{GCF}$ of the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\text{GCF}(2{x}^{2},2x)=2x\n$$\n\nThen, we rewrite each term in the original expression as a product with the $\\text{GCF}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+2x & = \\\\ (2x\\cdot x)+(2x\\cdot 1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we write the $\\text{GCF}$ outside the parentheses and keep the remaining terms inside:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2x\\cdot x)+(2x\\cdot 1) & = \\\\ 2x(x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we conclude that the length of the plot must be $2x$ meters.\n\n![](images/4c/4c27076821a19720b9038ab64552c85befa0c544e5295f1677b493ab36e6c9c9.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064328 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20900ac7-ad4e-5895-8d95-d66b0e5f7360" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Difference of Squares"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9d1d3d3-6f01-5e0f-a768-0cfa4a676349" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9d1d3d3-6f01-5e0f-a768-0cfa4a676349" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490894} :answer-field/id #uuid "1db74699-0e0e-516f-a37b-e6dc7f419536" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491016}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "23096ba0-8086-5e46-9af4-3a956927f2d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-133830" :question/problem "![](images/28/28400f096ff0d11258f5aa1f4c5afe7f2189d8f355c520d08b3dcfafb9e8e831.png)\n\nOlivia is Jacob's neighbor. She has a plot of land whose area is ${x}^{2}-1$ square meters and whose width is $x+1$ meters, as depicted above. What is the length of Olivia's plot in terms of $x?$\n\nOlivia's plot has a length of\n{{field-1}}\nmeters." :question/worked-solution "To find the length of Olivia's plot of land, we need to factor the expression ${x}^{2}-1.$\n\nFirst, we write the expression as a difference of squares:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-1={x}^{2}-{1}^{2}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor the expression using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-{1}^{2}=(x-1)(x+1)\n$$\n\nAs a result, we conclude that the length of the plot must be $x-1$ meters.\n\n![](images/20/20c00e624e31ab0cc4e4b44d4bddf0ec6255fdb674e1f7e2f483b6f53c98c909.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054775 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0b0b8a-3d45-5602-a842-a1b7f50ffcea" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1e91889-c904-5f8c-9474-ea776f1c6a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1e91889-c904-5f8c-9474-ea776f1c6a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490867} :answer-field/id #uuid "c332bba8-52a5-58c3-9d60-949adcb70443" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ef18d76-1c69-5646-b6be-0fad6315bf41" :question/math-academy-id "q-133831" :question/problem "![](images/87/87d9088567f74124a4af55333306d81d27cf41798a5411445b68ae0c8bc57550.png)\n\nA utility pole is located on the edge of Jacob's land, as shown above. The distance from the right edge of Jacob's plot to the pole is $x+1$ meters. Find the distance to the pole from the left edge as a function of $x.$\n\nThe required distance is \n{{field-1}}\nmeters." :question/worked-solution "In part 1, we found that the length of Jacob's plot is $2x$ meters.\n\nTo find the required distance, we need to subtract polynomials $2x$ and $x+1:$\n\nWe put a minus sign between the two polynomials, distribute it over the second polynomial, collect like terms, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2x)-(x+1) & = \\\\ 2x-x-1 & = \\\\ (2-1)x-1 & = \\\\ x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491186 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054659 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac258511-5028-5fc8-9843-99309b36a38e" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring Trinomials With Negative Constants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec61a87e-9a96-56fd-b489-b4024081d4b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec61a87e-9a96-56fd-b489-b4024081d4b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490961} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6fb5d65-68b8-5e66-b581-58fb181cc889" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491104}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9f4b7be-1158-5a94-a23c-150a70b64b99" :question/math-academy-id "q-133832" :question/problem "![](images/be/bef0863eeb7006d89cc92a80be2a84e6ea09bca14cbb29c15af4f2e01e79045f.png)\n\nJacob's neighbor to the south, Tom, has a land plot of area ${x}^{2}+x-2$ square meters, as shown in the picture. Given that the length of Tom's plot of land is $x-1$ meters, what is the width of the plot in terms of $x?$\n\nTom's plot width is\n{{field-1}}\nmeters." :question/worked-solution "To find the required width, we need to factor the expression ${x}^{2}+x-2.$\n\nFirst, we find the factor pairs of the constant term $(-2).$ The constant term is negative, so that means one of the factors is negative, and the other is positive:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & \\times (-2) \\\\ (-1) & \\times 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find which factor pair adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+(-2) & =-1 & \\times  \\\\ -1+2 & =1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the factor pair identified above, write the linear term as $x=2x-x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-2 & ={x}^{2}+2x-x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the first two terms and the last two terms separately, and then factor the expression completely:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x-x-2 & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2x)+(-x-2) & = \\\\ x(x+2)-(x+2) & = \\\\ (x-1)(x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we conclude that the width must be $x+2$ meters. \n\n![](images/d2/d2b543dc559c23c191231543701ffb05a7c8350bc066a047b836fe64766c7289.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491136 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078472 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa19126a-830f-5a11-a12b-2e150a520ecf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Degree of a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89e32882-43cb-5a38-98ef-9e8ab0f5817a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89e32882-43cb-5a38-98ef-9e8ab0f5817a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490787} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fe169dc-96d6-5da9-8c90-60bd8e17d082" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3fa06bfe-366e-54a8-ab4f-a6793fc21820" :question/math-academy-id "q-133833" :question/problem "What is the degree of the polynomial that represents the area of Tom's plot of land?\n\nDegree $\\,=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The polynomial \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+x-2\n$$\n\ncan be written as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{x}^{1}-2{x}^{0}.\n$$\n\nSo, it has the exponents $2,$ $1,$ and $0.$ The degree is the largest of these exponents, which is $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491165 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078531 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0f7a2ec-3d90-5930-bcc0-d51b8111dbe7" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44edaed4-d77d-5497-9983-08058b8e2c2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "154" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44edaed4-d77d-5497-9983-08058b8e2c2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "154" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490641} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e136489-d10a-5940-aea3-8d29829ada22" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "794c979f-c161-5b28-8239-699e664adb18" :question/math-academy-id "q-133834" :question/problem "If $x=12\\,\\text{m},$ what is the area of Tom's land plot?\n\nArea $\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we have to evaluate the polynomial ${x}^{2}+x-2$ at $x=12.$\n\nSo, we substitute $x=12$ into the polynomial and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-2 & = \\\\ (12)^{2}+(12)-2 & = \\\\ 144+12-2 & = \\\\ 154\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area is $154\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068679 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42cc9880-912e-5dce-9b93-e6af88a411c4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Length of the Hypotenuse Given the Length of the Legs of a Right Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63bc07cc-afae-5196-b92d-d648e0165e8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{317}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63bc07cc-afae-5196-b92d-d648e0165e8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{317}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490698} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea019c4b-31e8-554d-821b-4c2a12beacbe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491098}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "82932d5f-4a58-5db1-a173-dc03ee3fc19c" :question/math-academy-id "q-133835" :question/problem "![](images/e5/e5553b66879dcd4f8852f95d206e806b1ca378d8ca3e33cd9aeb3fc13bd22bed.png)\n\nWhen $x=12\\,\\text{m},$ the dimensions of Tom's plot of land are $11\\,\\text{m}$ and $14\\text{m}.$ A water pipe goes diagonally from one corner to the opposite, as shown above. Find the **exact** length of the pipe.\n\nThe length of the pipe is \n{{field-1}}\nmeters." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we have a right triangle with legs $a=11\\,\\text{m}$ and $b=14\\,\\text{m}.$\n\n![](images/87/87aee6e1c4071aa7efe82c19ffc6803f8f95a1b4e9108e0844b00593bc37434e.png)\n\nLet $c$ be the length of the hypotenuse. Then, according to the Pythagorean theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}^{2} & ={a}^{2}+{b}^{2} \\\\ c & =\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the values for $a$ and $b$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\sqrt{{11}^{2}+{14}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{121+196} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{317}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110626 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcd3e634-d64c-57dc-9d4c-8f7f67c731ab" :knowledge-point/title "Creating an Exponential Growth Expression Using Percentage Growth"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39ff3dce-35ba-55d4-927d-a8dbbe4081e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "245" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39ff3dce-35ba-55d4-927d-a8dbbe4081e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "245" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490617} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9fdea53-0db0-55cb-a27c-324b21367093" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491097}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "693e07af-f6f3-53ec-97e8-593deb89d0fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-133836" :question/problem "Jacob purchased his land for $180$ thousand dollars. The value of the land increases by $8%$ each year. How much will Jacob's plot be worth after $4$ years? Round your answer to the nearest thousand dollars.\n\nAfter $4$ years, the land will be worth approximately \n{{field-1}}\n thousand dollars." :question/worked-solution "The land initially costs $$180$ thousand, which increases at a rate of $8%$ per year.\n\n$8%$ as a decimal is $0.08.$ Therefore, an increase of $8%$ corresponds to multiplication by a factor of\n\n$$\n1+0.08=1.08.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n* After $1$ year, the value will be $180\\cdot (1.08)$ thousand dollars\n\n* After $2$ years, the value will be $180\\cdot (1.08)^{2}$ thousand dollars\n\n* After $3$ years, the value will be $180\\cdot (1.08)^{3}$ thousand dollars\n\n* After $4$ years, the value will be $180\\cdot (1.08)^{4}$ thousand dollars\n\nEvaluating the expression for the value after $4$ years, we get the following:\n\n$$\n180\\cdot (1.08)^{4}=244.88≈245,\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nTherefore, after $4$ years, the land will be worth approximately $245$ thousand dollars."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491187 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147563 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "373d4839-72d8-57df-bc72-c3312629e29e" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Output of an Exponential Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66175cd1-f3d0-5f77-9fa5-d63d6f4a25e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66175cd1-f3d0-5f77-9fa5-d63d6f4a25e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490703} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3a39b85-95f6-5f09-b603-5917e29c9cdb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ad0f9fe2-8f77-5646-944a-afdf1267d3bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-133837" :question/problem "The value $V(t)$ of Jacob's plot of land, in thousands of dollars, can be modeled by the function $V(t)=180\\cdot (1.08)^{t},$ where $t$ is the time in years since he bought the land. What is the growth in the value of the plot over the first two years? Round your answer to the nearest thousand dollars.\n\nJacob's land grew in value by approximately\n{{field-1}}\n thousand dollars over the first two years." :question/worked-solution "To find the growth in the value over the first two years, we need to find the value after $2$ years and then subtract the initial cost:\n\n$$\nV(2)-V(0)\n$$\n\nIn the previous part, we were given the initial value of the land:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V(0) & =180\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find $V(2),$ the value of the land after $2$ years:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V(2) & =180\\cdot (1.08)^{(2)} \\\\  & =180\\cdot (1.166\\,4) \\\\  & =209.952\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the growth in the first two years is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V(2)-V(0) & =209.952-180 \\\\  & =29.952 \\\\  & ≈30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the growth in the value of the land over the first two years was approximately $30$ thousand dollars."}]}
